# Line endings.
#
# This repository had no .gitattributes and `core.autocrlf = true` on the
# development machine, so every checkout rewrote LF to CRLF in the working
# tree while the repository itself stored LF. Mostly that is invisible. It
# stopped being invisible here:
#
#   `cargo run -p maya-neural-gas-trainer -- --check` compares
#   `crates/fee-market/src/model/weights_v1.rs` byte for byte against a fresh run of
#   the generator. The generator writes LF. A Windows checkout produced CRLF.
#   The check could therefore never pass on a fresh clone, and the one thing
#   standing between the compiled-in integer weights and a silent edit was
#   failing for a reason that has nothing to do with the weights.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises in the repository, as before, and now also
# checks out LF regardless of anyone's `core.autocrlf`. That also makes the
# working tree match what the Linux CI runners see.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the exception: cmd.exe requires CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary, never normalised. `text=auto` would usually detect these, but saying
# so is cheaper than trusting detection on a PNG that happens to look textual.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.wasm binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# Served byte-for-byte; joiners check its SHA-256, so no line-ending conversion.
docs/site/public/testnet/genesis.json -text
